; Spike 5: what the broker's deny-default profile allows beyond what the driver generates (the broker's own folder,
; node, Playwright, Chrome's bundle, the lane's ports). Add rules ONE at a time from the denial stream until
; broker_page_on_loopback passes for branded Chrome, each with a one-line reason. Never add: mach-register,
; appleevent-send, the pasteboard, securityd or Keychain services, launchd job submission (ServiceManagement, smd),
; LaunchServices (launchservicesd, lsd), camera or microphone services, any wildcard or prefix rule for mach-lookup,
; network-outbound or file-*, or any write under $HOME. The reviewed result becomes the lane's broker.sb.tmpl.

; Homebrew node links its libraries from here (read only).
(allow file-read* (subpath "/opt/homebrew/Cellar") (subpath "/opt/homebrew/opt") (subpath "/usr/local/Cellar") (subpath "/usr/local/opt"))


; Found by bisection on the Mac (2026-10-08, chromium-headless-shell 1243): without this the shell crashes at start
; (SIGSEGV, no log line); preference reads, the setup flag, disk-space info and DiskArbitration were each not needed.
; Most likely Chromium's power monitor (sleep/wake state); that attribution is an inference.
(allow iokit-open-user-client (iokit-user-client-class "RootDomainUserClient"))

; EXCEPTION to the never-list (mach-register, and a pattern rule), for the reviewer to accept or refuse explicitly.
; Chromium's multi-process design registers one rendezvous service per browser process to hand ports to its
; children: base/apple/mach_port_rendezvous_mac.cc:159 is FATAL without it ("bootstrap_check_in
; org.chromium.Chromium.MachPortRendezvousServer.<pid>: Permission denied"). The pid varies, so it must be a pattern:
; anchored, digits only, Chromium's own name only. It cannot match any Apple service.
(allow mach-register (global-name-regex #"^org\.chromium\.Chromium\.MachPortRendezvousServer\.[0-9]+$"))
; The other half: the children look up the service their parent registered.
(allow mach-lookup (global-name-regex #"^org\.chromium\.Chromium\.MachPortRendezvousServer\.[0-9]+$"))
